+# ---- decode / small row counts: one fused split-K kernel (gather by slot + fp8 -> bf16 + online softmax), after the
+# trellis CUDA lane's qsa_decode_triton.py (1523a13), reading the paged cache through token_slots instead of a packed
+# copy. The reference path above ran ~35 kernels per layer: 136 us per layer in a decode graph on the B70.
